{"link":{"rel":"self","url":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/item/655ceb8ad34ee4b6e05cc51a"},"relatedItems":{"link":{"url":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/itemLinks?itemId=655ceb8ad34ee4b6e05cc51a","rel":"related"}},"id":"655ceb8ad34ee4b6e05cc51a","identifiers":[{"type":"DOI","scheme":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/vocab/category/item/identifier","key":"doi:10.5066/P94UXNTS"}],"title":"Annual National Land Cover Database (NLCD) Collection 1 Products (ver. 1.1, June 2025)","summary":"The U.S. Geological Survey (USGS)’s Land Cover program has leveraged methodologies from legacy land cover projects - National Land Cover Database (NLCD) and Land Change Monitoring, Assessment, and Projection (LCMAP) - together with modern innovations in geospatial deep learning technologies to create the next generation of land cover and land change information. The product suite is called, “Annual NLCD” and includes six annual products that represent land cover and surface change characteristics of the U.S.:    Land Cover; Land Cover Change; Land Cover Confidence; Fractional Impervious Surface; Impervious Descriptor; and Spectral Change Day of Year.  These land cover science algorithms harness the remotely sensed Landsat data record [...]","body":"The U.S. Geological Survey (USGS)’s Land Cover program has leveraged methodologies from legacy land cover projects - National Land Cover Database (NLCD) and Land Change Monitoring, Assessment, and Projection (LCMAP) - together with modern innovations in geospatial deep learning technologies to create the next generation of land cover and land change information. The product suite is called, “Annual NLCD” and includes six annual products that represent land cover and surface change characteristics of the U.S.:<br>\n&nbsp;\n<ol>\n\t<li>Land Cover;<\/li>\n\t<li>Land Cover Change;<\/li>\n\t<li>Land Cover Confidence;<\/li>\n\t<li>Fractional Impervious Surface;<\/li>\n\t<li>Impervious Descriptor; and<\/li>\n\t<li>Spectral Change Day of Year.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\nThese land cover science algorithms harness the remotely sensed Landsat data record to provide the land surface change information needed by scientists, resource managers, and decision-makers. Annual NLCD uses a modernized, integrated approach to map, monitor, synthesize, and understand the complexities of land use, cover, and condition change.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\nQuestions about the Annual NLCD product suite can be directed to the Annual NLCD mapping team at USGS EROS, Sioux Falls, SD (605) 594-6151 or custserv@usgs.gov. See included spatial metadata for more details.","citation":"U.S. Geological Survey (USGS), 2024, Annual NLCD Collection 1 Science Products (ver. 1.1, June 2025): U.S. Geological Survey data release, https://doi.org/10.5066/P94UXNTS.","purpose":"The goal of this project is to provide the Nation with complete, current, and consistent public domain information on its land use and land cover.","rights":"This work is marked with Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). This work is marked with Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). ","provenance":{"annotation":"To review the changes that were made, see \"RevisonHistory_v1.1.txt\" file in the attached files section. Revision 1.1 by Audra Griebel on June 25, 2025.\n2026-03-17: The structure of this data release has been updated to support migration to a new USGS data system. No changes were made to the data during this update.","dateCreated":"2023-11-21T17:40:26Z","lastUpdated":"2026-06-16T19:11:22Z"},"hasChildren":true,"parentId":"5f10965282ce21d4c40796be","contacts":[{"name":"U.S. Geological Survey","type":"Point of Contact","contactType":"organization","organization":{},"primaryLocation":{"streetAddress":{},"mailAddress":{}}},{"name":"U.S. Geological Survey","oldPartyId":18139,"type":"Originator","contactType":"organization","onlineResource":"http://www.usgs.gov/","active":true,"aliases":[